'''Namua''' was a [[Nautolan]] [[Gender|male]] who lived on the ''[[Colossus]]'' platform in [[34 ABY]]. He sold fruit at the [[Colossus marketplace|''Colossus'' marketplace]]. He had an inquisitive personality, and was present for several major events on the station.

==Biography==
{{Quote|Hey look! It's Torra Doza|Namua|<ref name="Secrets and Holograms" />}}
In [[34 ABY]], Namua watched the [[Race between Kazuda Xiono and Torra Doza|race]] between [[Torra Doza]], and the newcomer [[Kazuda Xiono]], from his fruit stall.<ref name="Recruit">{{Resistance|The Recruit}}</ref> During his efforts to spy on Colussus residents, Kazuda used Namua's stall as cover. When the Colossus was [[Attack on the Colossus|raided by pirates]], Namua hid in a shelter until the [[pirate]]s retreated.<ref name="Triple Dark">{{Resistance|The Triple Dark}}</ref> He was walking the corridors when Xiono ran down to try and save [[Jace Rucklin]].<ref name="Fuel for Fire">{{Resistance|Fuel for the Fire}}</ref> Namua was also working at his store when the [[droid]] [[BB-8]] was searching for Xiono.<ref name="Search for Kaz">{{Resistance|The Search for Kaz}}</ref>

When the pirates [[Raid on the Colossus|attacked]] again, Namua went to salvage the content of a hoverlift that had been rammed into the pirate [[Leoz]].<ref name="Synara's Score">{{Resistance|Synara's Score}}</ref> Sometime after, Namua was in the market and spotted [[Torra Doza]], daughter of ''Colossus'' [[Captain]] [[Imanuel Doza]]. He and a few others bombarded her with questions about what Doza was doing regarding [[pirate]] attacks and canceled races.<ref name="Secrets and Holograms" />

When the [[First Order]] occupied the Colossus, Namua was among the residents who protested against them in the marketplace. Later that same day, as he was walking through the station, Namua came across [[Neeku Vozo|Neeku]], [[Tamara Ryvora|Tam]], [[BB-8]], [[Kel]], and [[Eila]], who were carrying an unconscious [[First Order stormtrooper|stormtrooper]]. He asked about the stormtrooper's wellbeing, but seemingly accepted their explanation that the man was ill.<ref name="The New Trooper">{{Resistance|The New Trooper}}</ref>

When the food stores on the Colossus ran out while the station was fleeing from the First Order, [[Z'Vk'Thkrkza|Aunt Z]] declared that she was leaving, and several other residents, including Namua, volunteered to join her. However, Namua and the others were convinced to stay when Kazuda and Torra successfully hunted down a [[jakoosk]] to feed the station. When Neeku rigged up a [[hologram]] to simulate [[Castilon]]'s sky outside the marketplace, Namua exclaimed that it looked just like the real thing.<ref name="Hunt on Celsor 3">{{Resistance|Hunt on Celsor 3}}</ref>

==Personality and traits==
Namua was a [[Gender|male]] [[Nautolan]] with [[Color|green]] skin and black eyes. The tentacles on his head were short, and he kept them tied back in a ponytail.<ref name="Secrets and Holograms" />

He paid close attention to what was happening on the Colossus, and was sometimes inquisitive to the point of being invasive.<ref name="Databank">{{Databank|namua|Namua}}</ref>

==Behind the scenes==
Namua first appeared in "[[The Recruit]]," the first episode of ''[[Star Wars Resistance]] [[Star Wars Resistance Season One|Season One]]''.<ref name="Recruit" /> He was first identified in "[[Secrets and Holograms]]," where he was voiced by [[Stephen Stanton]].<ref name="Secrets and Holograms" />

